# Silverpine Forest - Completionist (pack butler-routes-completionist, v1).
# The pack's first HORDE route: every Silverpine accept in the local census
# (68 quests, docs/silverpine-census.md) appears exactly once as an accept
# and once as a turnin. Band 10-20 by minLevel cluster (zone id 1421, order
# 33). The 5 Alliance-only records, 34 repeatables, 3 seasonal/events and 12
# above-band records are out with reasons in the census, plus the Tirisfal
# accept 361 and Arathi's pendant 635 (home-zone owns; no double-contract).
# No race header: Undead, Orc, Tauren and Troll all play this route, with
# per-line gates where the data is exclusive - only Undead (races=16;
# token Undead per the format doc) on the Sepulcher-only lines and the
# Paladin line's Undead legs, only Shaman on Call of Water, only Rogue on
# the Horn of Xelthos, only Paladin on the Earthen Ring line (cls=2;
# Shaman impossible for races=16, classic bitmask confirms). No profession
# quests in contract (every skill field null) - stated, not padded. Soft-pre
# accepts whose blocking pre-quest sits outside the contract (446 Tirisfal
# for 448, 63 Barrens for 100, 91858 Tirisfal for 91859, 95126 Hillsbrad
# for 95140) carry a note at the accept; their turn-ins stand alone in when
# onquest mini-steps. R2 bag-note records (no source anywhere in the data):
# 422's Remedy, 450's journal, 1103's sapta, 5725's books, the Digest and
# Secrets volumes, 95036's crafted materials, 95140's blade, 95216's strain.
# Dungeon work (Arugal's head, the Horn of Xelthos) rides bare completes
# with a Shadowfang Keep note - the data holds seven scattered same-name
# portal objects and none verifies as the entrance, so no point is
# invented. Expedition turn-ins: Tirisfal (Sevren), Undercity (Zinge,
# Bethor, Wendham, Owen Thadd), Hillsbrad (Lydon, Ott), Barrens (Islen),
# plus a Westfall expedition for 91920's murloc eyes (no in-zone dropper).
# No loop steps: every placed complete rides data-placed coordinates.
guide butler-routes-completionist/silverpine-forest
title Silverpine Forest - Completionist
levels 10-20
zone Silverpine Forest
faction Horde
category Leveling
folder Completionist
coords live
version 1

step The Sepulcher - the Forsaken hub

  zone map 1421

  note The Sepulcher holds the route's hub: Hadrec (43.42,40.86), Renferrel (42.8,40.86), Dalar (44.2,39.81), Allister (43.98,40.93), Podrig (43.42,41.68), Karos (45.62,42.6), Trevan (43.4,41.1), Baldren (45.81,41.88) and Lumina (43.4,40.99).
  accept 428 -- Lost Deathstalkers - Hadrec; find Quinn and Rane at the Ivar Patch north
  accept 437 -- The Dead Fields - Hadrec; rot hide gnolls west, Nightlash shows herself
  accept 447 -- A Recipe For Death - Renferrel; grizzled hearts and skittering blood, west woods
  accept 477 -- Border Crossings - Allister; a Dalaran crate waits in Pyrewood south
  accept 421 -- Prove Your Worth - Dalar; Moonrage whitescalps, north-west dens
  accept 448 -- Report to Hadrec - Renferrel; a pointer with no field work (note 446 Thule Ravenclaw accepts in Tirisfal, not contracted here - the turn-in rides the mini-step below)
  accept 6321 only Undead -- Supplying the Sepulcher - Deathguard Podrig; carry the order to Karos Razok
  turnin 6321 only Undead -- Supplying the Sepulcher - the order to Karos Razok
  accept 6323 only Undead -- Ride to the Undercity - Karos Razok; take the order to Gordon Wendham in Undercity (expedition below)
  accept 1014 -- Arugal Must Die - Dalar Dawnweaver; Arugal's head sits inside Shadowfang Keep (dungeon note below)
  accept 1098 -- Deathstalkers in Shadowfang - Hadrec; find Adamant and Vincent (Vincent has no placed spawn - honest note below)
  accept 493 -- Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills - Renferrel; findings for Lydon in Tarren Mill (Hillsbrad expedition below)
  accept 91859 only Paladin -- A Curious Pair - Trevan; speak with Deathguard Baldren (note 91858 Diplomatic Incident accepts in Tirisfal, not contracted here - the turn-in rides the mini-step below)
  accept 516 -- Beren's Peril - Allister; Ravenclaw drudgers and guardians at Beren's Peril south (below)

